# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Lecture 50 vignette pool B -- Hematologic Malignancies Part II: non-Hodgkin lymphoma (s15-34): indolent types
(follicular, marginal zone, lymphoplasmacytic), aggressive and T-cell types, risk, work-up, Lugano (Ann Arbor) staging
from the node map (s26 picture), management, tumor lysis syndrome, poor-prognosis factor counts (s30), Burkitt
lymphoma and patient education. Every slide in the range viewed at 1920 px.

KEYS ARE WRITTEN SHORT ON PURPOSE -- detail lives in the explanation.
EXPLANATIONS follow tools/question_writing/EXPLAIN_DEEP.md.

Staging stems name node regions and organs only as the s26 picture captions read: stage 1 a single node region or
single organ; stage 2 two or more node regions on the same side of the diaphragm; stage 3 node regions above and
below the diaphragm; stage 4 widespread disease, multiple organs, with or without nodes.
Poor-prognosis counts use the s30 list as written (age over 60, extranodal sites, performance status above 2, stage
III or IV, elevated lactate dehydrogenase); no stem sits at age 60 or performance status 2.
Laboratory ranges in the tumor lysis stems are standard adult reference ranges and only set the scene.
"""
import os, sys
sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
